[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. It is more than one problem.
The desk merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and
every report says the same thing: the date is wrong. The bodies, the tenants and their booking
forms say why, and the why is not the same.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

<Callout>
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. `parser` is fixed: fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu
locales. `hint` won't be fixed: the `booking-v3` form is retired.
</Callout>

## The problems

**`parser`: day and month swap.** The shared parser reads every date month first, and every
tenant in #4471 writes the day first. "Our 7 April reminder went out on 4 July." It reaches
every tenant through the app, email and the `booking-v2` form. Fixed: parse dd/mm for eu locales.

**`hint`: the form tells people to type it wrong.** `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under
its date field and then reads the date day first. People do what the hint says, and the date
swaps. Only the tenants on `booking-v3`, only through the form. The symptom is the same as
`parser`, so the subject rule merged it. The fix is not the same, and it had no ticket of its
own: the desk's table below already marks the row "not this ticket". Won't fix: the form is retired.

**The one-day moves.** The desk read a few `parser` reports as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`). Their tenant files them under `parser`, so they are counted there, once,
and footnoted under the table.

## How to read the counts

- One id, one report: the export repeats some reports, so the table counts unique ids.
- The tenant decides the problem, not intake's tag. Intake's tag is a guess from the browser,
  and it disagrees with the tenant on dozens of reports (see the table below).
- Every number on this page is computed at render time from the export. None is typed.

